1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,165
In November 1937, a Chinese general promised to live or die with his capital.

2
00:00:06,769 --> 00:00:09,741
Less than four weeks later the capital was gone,

3
00:00:09,985 --> 00:00:12,144
and he was on the other side of the river.

4
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:15,499
This is how Nanjing became a trap.

5
00:00:16,103 --> 00:00:18,158
It starts two hundred miles away,

6
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:19,284
in Shanghai.

7
00:00:19,795 --> 00:00:24,102
For three months China throws its best divisions into that city.

8
00:00:24,613 --> 00:00:26,668
In November the line breaks.

9
00:00:27,109 --> 00:00:29,780
The Japanese army was sent to take Shanghai.

10
00:00:30,105 --> 00:00:32,125
Its commanders do not stop there.

11
00:00:32,821 --> 00:00:36,420
A hundred and sixty thousand men chase the retreat west,

12
00:00:36,571 --> 00:00:38,881
up the Yangtze, toward the capital.

13
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,933
Nanjing has been China's capital for ten years.

14
00:00:43,537 --> 00:00:47,891
That spring the city counted one million and nineteen thousand people.

15
00:00:48,494 --> 00:00:51,536
By December most of those who could leave have left.

16
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:56,180
Somewhere between a quarter and half a million are still inside.

17
00:00:56,680 --> 00:01:00,116
Around them is a wall thirty-five kilometres long.

18
00:01:00,546 --> 00:01:02,113
Behind it is the river.

19
00:01:02,485 --> 00:01:05,259
A kilometre of water, and no bridge.

20
00:01:06,061 --> 00:01:10,008
Most of China's generals want to give the city up and save the army.

21
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:12,818
Chiang Kai-shek refuses.

22
00:01:13,259 --> 00:01:15,059
He moves the government inland,

23
00:01:15,209 --> 00:01:18,948
and gives the city to the one general who says it can be held.

24
00:01:19,761 --> 00:01:24,103
That general has between seventy and a hundred and fifty thousand men.

25
00:01:24,915 --> 00:01:26,796
Nobody agrees on the number.

26
00:01:27,307 --> 00:01:28,968
Half of them are recruits.

27
00:01:29,409 --> 00:01:31,115
So he takes away their way out.

28
00:01:31,499 --> 00:01:32,950
He walls up the gates.

29
00:01:33,275 --> 00:01:35,225
He sends the ferries upriver.

30
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:40,125
On December the eighth, the last line outside the city breaks.

31
00:01:40,636 --> 00:01:44,931
By the next morning seventy thousand Japanese soldiers are at the wall,

32
00:01:45,047 --> 00:01:46,243
on three sides.

33
00:01:46,754 --> 00:01:48,762
On the fourth side is the river.

